    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="6">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hl">Hl</ref> 6</head>
        <ab type="selectedText" xml:lang="und">Gif ceorle acwyle be libbendum wife ⁊ bearne, riht is þæt hit, þæt bearn, medder folgige, ⁊ him man an his fæderingmagum wilsumne berigean ge[s]elle his feoh to healdenne, oþ þæt he X wintra sie.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en">If a freeman should die with a living wife and child, it is right that it, that child, should be under the protection of the mother, and one should give for him one among his father’s kin who willingly gives surety to maintain his property, until he should be 10 years old.</ab>
        <ab type="supplementaryText" xml:lang="und">Gif ceorle acwyle be libbendum wife ⁊ bearne, riht is þæt hit, þæt bearn, medder folgige, ⁊ him mon an his fæderingmagum wilsumne berigean gefelle, his feoh to healdenne, oþ þæt he X wintra sie.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
